  "state_model": "512 training-only stable nonpanel genes; per-source/lane NTC centering/scaling; 8 PCA coordinates and 4 shared KMeans states. Complete outer study excluded from stable-gene selection, PCA, KMeans and source responses. Recipient NTCs only calibrate their own lane transform.",
  "mechanism": "Original V52 disjoint treatment/control views per lane. Smoothed state density ratios and within-state CPM log2FC; abundance shrink n/(n+32), within-state shrink state_n/(state_n+16). States from treated RNA can retain response. No observed individual counterfactual or birth/death claim.",
  "oracle": "Fit one complete matched population view and reconstruct the other using its controls; compute response error only AFTER population aggregation. V59/V60 lane-error diagnostic was underpowered and cannot be compared numerically with this population-level error. Earlier scores and files remain intact.",
  "transfer": "Same-target source mechanisms; one total vote per study, reliability and nonpanel basal Spearman weighting. Measured masks prevent missing genes voting zero. Fixed primary joint50. Diagnostic composition50/pooled50. Within-source cyclic target derangement is negative control. All comparators use saved V58 baseline arrays; H1/Orion additionally exclude CD4 in these inherited comparator arrays, while held-CD4 comparator matches earlier tests.",
  "release": "Require fixed joint50 equal-study mean MSE gain >=1%, no study >2% worse, beat shuffled and pooled each study. Counts must improve expression MSE and two DE metrics, no CD4 FID/JAC regression >.005, beat shuffle. Public repeatedly examined biology; no hidden-score guarantee. D3 unopened. Failed candidates cannot be labeled improved or silently replace V24.",
  "counts": "44 fixed target-seed populations, common real rows/seeds across arms; unchanged V24 residual10 emitter for mean comparisons. New aggregate means permitted. State-cell diagnostic uses actual NTCs and conditional balanced count edits, without enforcing old means.",
  "literature": [
    {
      "title": "Milo",
      "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-021-01033-z"
    },
    {
      "title": "muscat",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33257685/"
    }
  ],
  "D3_opened": false,
  "automatically_upload": false,
  "parent_plan_sha256": "16423f0a9c4a6e43207f70a95e850d7312918a6f480c0171c96fcf8b8a74622f",
  "parent_CPM_correction_sha256": "5743d1015642cc948abfdfbd25b7e003d686a54bac6a418202d7b1b16c1fa375",
  "parent_mask_correction_sha256": "406663c0f6dc474bfe54557854b3badb2e608721215782e5f1220b27fe7a48e8",
  "state_adjustment": "NTC-only lane-specific ridge of log1p(CPM) on centered/scaled log nonpanel raw depth, log nonpanel detected-gene count, their squares and interaction; intercept unpenalized, other ridge .1. Divide residual by NTC residual SD floor .5 and clip +/-5. All 300 panel genes excluded from nuisance covariates. Source fold gene selection, PCA, KMeans, response/shuffle/decoder methods and release gates unchanged.",
  "reason": "Some V52 target/lane views have only two treated cells. Estimating/shrinking each lane-state effect before pooling nearly erases the response. The alternative pools the sufficient statistics while retaining batch/state matched controls.",
  "version_selection": "V60 primary joint50 and gates fixed before V60 state/treatment outcomes. Compare with V59 descriptively; do not select diagnostic arms post hoc. No claim that all original abundance structure was technical.",
  "raw_cache_reuse": {
    "H1": "e2e4111ecc0bf8bf658a2d9939ef775324d9b80c41d871c84e2e1ea4ae9f47ab",
    "HCT116": "56355ea9afd4f491d1137436dec6a860eb42205f9060ad623db7a1ac54ebac73",
    "HEK293T": "88888f650f4e37d5754105dbe7241d94578eb1c43feb4d62d4e0a6bc161d812d",
    "CD4_Rest_D2": "686a0b0338f53691ead288ef38a8fe887a8560a98770e84691b34a12ed62cf62",
    "CD4_Stim48_D2": "0d0586707c9f3e9b271d4a516e05a3ef902dc8c86a244875e11699b1b69237ee"
  },
  "pooling": "Within each target/view, pool treated state counts/sums and matched-lane control state means before estimating nonlinear ratios/shrinkage. Conditional controls weight each lane by treated counts in that state. Abundance controls weight each lane by its total treated count and NTC state frequency, rescaled to actual sampled NTC total for density pseudocounts. Two view mechanisms combine with treated-state count weights. No recipient labels enter transfer.",
  "release_candidate": "Fixed V61 joint50 primary; diagnostic arms cannot be selected post hoc. V59/V60 retained as independent comparators. A user-requested experimental upload file, if generated after failed gates, must explicitly report failure and cannot be labeled improved or overwrite V24."
}
